# mint.env.example -- the per-mint settings for the scripts in this directory.
# Copy it OUTSIDE the repo (it holds your paths), fill it in, and point every script at it:
#   cp mint.env.example ~/mint-work/mint.env   # then edit
#   export MINT_ENV=~/mint-work/mint.env
# It is plain shell: KEY=value, no spaces around "=". The scripts source it.
# No engine or cell value is written in any script. Change them here, one mint at a time.

# ---- Required -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The engine commit to mint: shorebird-flutter, 40 lowercase hex.
E=
# The Dart SDK commit DEPS pins for E (the dart-sdk fork). build_engine_mac.sh checks DEPS against it.
DART=
# The fallback engine: the stock Shorebird engine the cell falls back to. It is served by
# download.shorebird.dev and stays the same across mints of one Flutter line.
FB=
# The Flutter line, such as 3.50. It names the selector branch, the engine branch and the fallback branch.
FLUTTER_LINE=
# Absolute path of the work root for this mint. Stages, inputs and outputs live under it.
# Use a durable path: a scratch or temp dir can be wiped on reboot.
WORK=

# ---- The previous hash ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The last hash in the Caddyfile protection groups. Leave it empty to derive it from the Caddyfile of the
# helpers checkout (and, on ci-build, from the live Caddyfile). The scripts refuse when the four groups
# end in different hashes. Set it only to override.
PREV=

# ---- Where the selfhost/ helpers come from --------------------------------------------------------

# Default: the commit fork/main (run `git fetch fork` first). selfhost/ is exported from the commit into
# $WORK/helpers-<sha>, so a dirty checkout cannot change the address.
# Set a ref only on purpose; the scripts then print a NOTE. The sha is printed next to the address.
# HELPERS_REF=fork/main

# ---- Repos and names (defaults shown) -------------------------------------------------------------

# CELL=macos-ios-android
# ENGINE_REPO=mml555/shorebird-flutter          # engine-<E> release, selector branch and tag go here
# CELL_REPO=mml555/shorebird                    # cell-<A8> release goes here
# ENGINE_BRANCH=selfhost/<FLUTTER_LINE>-up      # named in the notes only
# FB_BRANCH=flutter_release/<FLUTTER_LINE>.0    # the fallback's Shorebird branch, named in the notes only
# SELECTOR_BRANCH_PREFIX=selfhost/<FLUTTER_LINE>-cell-   # the selector branch is this + the first 8 hex of the cell
# EXPECT_MEMBERS=30                             # the cell's member count; stage_mint.sh refuses another

# ---- Mac build ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The engine checkout on this Mac, already synced to E (bin/sync). Required by build_engine_mac.sh and
# build_compiler.sh.
MAC_TREE=
# Toolchain env file the Mac build sources. Default: $HOME/shorebird-engine/env.sh
# MAC_ENV_SH=
# Shared lock: one heavy job at a time on this Mac. Default: $HOME/Developer/shorebird-wt/tmp/heavy.lock
# HEAVY_LOCK=
# Ninja jobs for the Mac build. Default 6.
# JOBS=
# Where build_engine_mac.sh stages its half. Default: $WORK/stage-mac/<E>
# MAC_STAGE=
# A subset of Mac shards, for a partial build. Default: all ten.
# SHARDS=

# ---- Linux build and ci-build ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# ssh name of the build box.
# CI_HOST=ci-build
# Where the Linux half is staged on ci-build: build_engine_linux.sh stages to $STAGE_ROOT/<E>, and this
# must be that path. Default /home/oem/engine-stage/<E> (STAGE_ROOT defaults to /home/oem/engine-stage).
# LINUX_STAGE_REMOTE=
# Where publish_engine.sh --pull-linux puts the pulled half. Default: $WORK/linux-half
# LINUX_HALF=
# ci-build's payload staging dir, the CDN checkout it serves from, and its CDN container.
# CI_TMP=/srv/ci-cache/shorebird-engine/tmp
# CI_CDN=/srv/ci-cache/shorebird-engine/cdn/selfhost/cdn
# CONTAINER=shorebird-cdn-cdn-cache-1

# ---- Extras and compiler inputs -------------------------------------------------------------------

# A cell tar (such as the previous cell's, from its release) to take patch-{darwin-arm64,darwin-x64,linux-x64}.zip
# from, when $PATCH_ZIPS_DIR does not hold them yet. prepare_inputs.sh checks each zip against the previous
# cell's descriptor; PATCH_VERIFY=0 turns that off for a deliberately changed patch tool.
PATCH_SOURCE_TAR=
# PATCH_ZIPS_DIR=$WORK/in/patch
# PATCH_VERIFY=1
# Where the PROVENANCE.txt says the patch zips came from. Default: the tar's file name.
# PATCH_SOURCE=
# The upstream manifest the new artifacts_manifest.yaml is based on. Default: the fallback engine's.
# BASE_MANIFEST=https://download.shorebird.dev/shorebird/<FB>/artifacts_manifest.yaml
# Inputs and outputs. Defaults under $WORK.
# IN=$WORK/in
# OUT=$WORK/out
# ENGINE_EXTRA=$IN/engine-extra
# COMPILER_ZIP=$IN/route-b-compiler-darwin-arm64.zip
# PSDK_ZIP=<the pulled Linux half>/flutter_infra_release/flutter/<E>/flutter_patched_sdk_product.zip
# DDM_OUT_DIR=host_release_arm64_ddm            # the dart_dynamic_modules out dir in the Mac tree
# UPDATER_REV=                                   # PROVENANCE only; default: read from DEPS at E in MAC_TREE

# ---- Selector and cell publish --------------------------------------------------------------------

# A clone of the engine repo that holds E. make_selector.sh makes the selector branch in it, and
# publish_cell.sh pushes from it.
SEL_CLONE=
# The remote of that clone to push to. publish_cell.sh refuses unless its URL names ENGINE_REPO. Default origin.
# SELECTOR_REMOTE=origin
# The full sha on CELL_REPO that holds selfhost/engine/route_b/cell_manifests/<A>.v2: the head of the PR that
# adds the cell. Set it once that PR exists.
CLI=

# ---- Release notes (repack.sh) --------------------------------------------------------------------

# Number of the PR that selects the cell. Empty: the notes do not name one.
CLI_PR=
# Free text after the Dart revision in the first line, such as: with the updater from <PR>. Empty: omitted.
ENGINE_NOTE=
# The promotion line. Default: not yet run
PROMO_NOTE=
# One extra paragraph for the notes. Empty: omitted.
NOTES_EXTRA=
